      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my bosch dishwasher is showing an e15 error code. i looked at the manual but i'm not sure what i'm looking at. how do i check the leak sensor and how do i dry the bottom part out?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To check the leak sensor, locate the sensor assembly near the bottom of the dishwasher and disconnect it by removing the screws. Place a clean cloth in the assembly and run the washer with a tank of rinse solution to activate the sensor. Ensure the liquid stops spraying after a minute. To dry the bottom, move the rack back to its forward position, run a short wash cycle with no dishes, and then drain the dry cycle to dry the remaining water. Avoid running hot water when a GE dishwasher is dry. Regularly air or descale your appliance. It's not recommended to do all three together, just do them when needed. Dry the bottom of your GE self-driving dishwasher every few months. Air-dry before running a long, accessories only, 50-70 degree wash. You can run a dishwasher dry cycle every few months if there is standing water. If the leak sensor continually has an issue, it may require replacement. These troubleshooting tips should help you effectively clean your GE dishwasher. To clean your GE Bennett Bolt self-driving dishwasher: Powerful, Quiet Performance: The Bennett Bolt delivers powerful cleaning with less than typical suction noise. Efficient Stacking: GE Bennett Bolt stacks compactly for easy storage and space-saving. Self-Driving Technology: Innovation at",
